on the flop, indicating a likely weak hand or a slow-played monster, though weakness is more probable given the dry board. You have the option to check for free. Folding is illogical when checking is available. Betting might fold out hands you are already beating (like Queen-high) but will likely be called by any pair (8s or 6s), putting you at a disadvantage.\n\nReason: Checking is the optimal play here. It controls the pot size and allows you to realize your equity by seeing the River card for free. If you hit a King or Jack on the river, you likely have the best hand. If the opponent is bluffing or has a weak hand, you may win at showdown with King-high. There is no strong strategic benefit to bloating the pot with a marginal hand like King-high.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
